[[File:Lamp (Beta 49.1).png|thumb|257x257px|Beta 49.1]]
Lamp was added in '''Beta 7.6''' as a 0/2 Taunt monster with a cost of 3G. Its cost was reduced to 2G in '''Beta 18.1''', and its HP was reduced by and to 1 in '''Beta 19.0'''. Both changes were reverted in '''Beta 32.1'''. '''Beta 36.1''' reduced its cost back to 2G.
[[File:Lamp (Beta 51.0).png|thumb|257x257px|Beta 51.0]]
Its Dust had a 0.5% chance to summon [[Frisk]]. '''Beta 49.1''' started changing what the other 99.5% summoned. From summoning a new 0-3G monster, it now no longer summoned another Lamp or 3G monsters. '''Beta 51.0''' changed to to summoning a 3-6G monster and set its (or Frisk's) stats to a base 2/2, while '''Beta 51.1''' removed the 6G monsters as well as Frisk from the possible summons, making the effect have a full 100% chance to summon a random 2/2 3-5G monster.
[[File:Lamp (Beta 51.1).png|thumb|Beta 51.1]]
The remaining randomness was removed in '''Beta 56.0''', where Lamp's effect was changed again, now summoning a Snow Frisk upon death, an effectless 2/2/2 exclusive Token. '''Beta 58.1''' removed Lamp's Taunt, in exchange for +1 ATK.
[[File:Lamp (Beta 56.0).png|thumb|Beta 56.0]]

